From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] jail: allow Mesa's shader cache and read+execute in the aarch64 GPU sandbox

With Ubuntu's Mesa on arm64, one logged pass over a VM with OpenGL
acceleration (first start, desktop, a GL client, shutdown) showed only
these sandbox failures, all at GPU start-up:
- fallocate (mode 0), flock and renameat from Mesa's shader disk cache
  (its index is 8 + 65536 * 32 bytes, preallocated with posix_fallocate);
- mprotect to a non-writable executable protection in the GPU worker.

Mesa 26.2 also compares the cache's recorded size with its file system
using statvfs, which is statfs on arm64: with that Mesa the GPU process
was killed while creating its GBM device.

Allow the cache calls as the x86_64 policy already does for Mesa's
cache, narrowed to plain allocation and to renameat (arm64 has no
rename), plus statfs, which the x86_64 policy lacks as well. Allow
mprotect to any protection without write. Writable and executable
together stays forbidden.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/jail/seccomp/aarch64/gpu_common.policy b/jail/seccomp/aarch64/gpu_common.policy
index 954cafb..303e329 100644
--- a/jail/seccomp/aarch64/gpu_common.policy
+++ b/jail/seccomp/aarch64/gpu_common.policy
@@ -83,7 +83,10 @@ ioctl: arg1 & 0x6400 || arg1 & 0x8000 || arg1 == 0x40086200 || arg1 == 0x4008754
 # example) with PROT_READ|PROT_EXEC|PROT_BTI and may apply it again with mprotect. Writable and
 # executable together stays forbidden.
 mmap: arg2 == PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE || arg2 == PROT_NONE || arg2 == PROT_READ|PROT_EXEC || arg2 == PROT_WRITE || arg2 == PROT_READ || arg2 == PROT_READ|PROT_EXEC|PROT_BTI
-mprotect: arg2 == PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE || arg2 == PROT_NONE || arg2 == PROT_READ || arg2 == PROT_READ|PROT_EXEC|PROT_BTI
+# The GPU worker also changes pages to read+execute (with or without BTI) at startup on arm64
+# (Ubuntu's Mesa, which loads LLVM). Allow any protection without write; writable and
+# executable together stays forbidden.
+mprotect: arg2 == PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE || arg2 in PROT_READ|PROT_EXEC|PROT_BTI
 openat: 1
 
 ## Rules specific to pvr
@@ -111,6 +114,14 @@ userfaultfd: 1
 # 0xc018aa3f == UFFDIO_API, 0xaa00 == USERFAULTFD_IOC_NEW
 ioctl: arg1 == 0xc018aa3f || arg1 == 0xaa00
 
+## Rules for Mesa's shader disk cache, as in the x86_64 policy and narrowed to what it uses
+## on arm64: preallocate the cache index (plain allocation only), lock it, move finished
+## entries into place, and compare the cache's recorded size with its file system (statvfs).
+fallocate: arg1 == 0
+flock: 1
+renameat: 1
+statfs: 1
+
 ## Rules for mali shader dump (debug workflow)
 mkdirat: 1
 
